ACC-011 — Engineering Capability

Document ID: ACC-011
Title: Engineering Capability
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines Engineering Capability, the reusable cognitive functions that Atlas performs using Engineering Understanding, Engineering Knowledge, Engineering Evidence, and Engineering Reasoning.

Engineering Capabilities represent the operational abilities of Atlas to perform engineering tasks in support of analysis, evaluation, prediction, validation, optimization, and decision support.

2. Scope

This specification applies to all engineering capabilities implemented within the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework.

Engineering Capabilities may include, but are not limited to:

Engineering analysis
Design validation
Code and standards compliance verification
Structural assessment
Risk assessment
Root cause analysis
Optimization
Simulation evaluation
Prediction
Recommendation generation
Change impact analysis
Quantity estimation
Cost estimation
Schedule analysis
Constructability assessment

This specification defines the concept of capability rather than specific capability implementations.

3. Canonical Definition

Engineering Capability is a reusable cognitive function that applies Engineering Understanding, Engineering Knowledge, Engineering Evidence, and Engineering Reasoning to accomplish a defined engineering objective.

Capabilities represent what Atlas can perform, not the data it stores or the reasoning process itself.

4. Characteristics

Engineering Capability SHALL possess the following characteristics.

4.1 Goal-Oriented

Every Engineering Capability SHALL pursue a defined engineering objective.

4.2 Cognition-Driven

Engineering Capability SHALL utilize Engineering Understanding as its primary cognitive input.

4.3 Evidence-Based

Engineering Capability SHALL rely upon Engineering Evidence where applicable.

4.4 Knowledge-Informed

Engineering Capability SHALL utilize relevant Engineering Knowledge when available.

4.5 Explainable

The outputs of an Engineering Capability SHALL be explainable through traceable reasoning and supporting evidence.

4.6 Context-Aware

Engineering Capability SHALL operate within an explicit engineering context.

4.7 Reusable

Engineering Capabilities SHALL be reusable across applicable engineering domains and projects.

4.8 Composable

Engineering Capabilities MAY be combined to create higher-level engineering workflows.

