Engineering Capability:

Uses Engineering Understanding.
Applies Engineering Reasoning.
References Engineering Knowledge.
Consumes Engineering Evidence.
Produces engineering outcomes.
Supports Decision Support.
6. Responsibilities

Engineering Capability is responsible for:

Performing engineering analyses.
Solving engineering problems.
Evaluating engineering alternatives.
Producing engineering recommendations.
Supporting engineering workflows.
Delivering reusable engineering functionality.
Maintaining explainability and traceability.
7. Normative Requirements

Engineering Capabilities SHALL:

Operate upon Engineering Understanding.
Utilize Engineering Reasoning.
Reference applicable Engineering Knowledge.
Preserve traceability to Engineering Evidence.
Produce explainable engineering outputs.
Support repeatable engineering execution.

Atlas SHALL NOT expose Engineering Capabilities that cannot provide sufficient engineering justification for their outputs.

8. Non-Goals

Engineering Capability does not:

Define Engineering Reality.
Replace Engineering Understanding.
Replace Engineering Reasoning.
Replace Engineering Knowledge.
Authorize engineering decisions.
Replace qualified engineering professionals.
9. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY define capability taxonomies, capability composition models, orchestration mechanisms, domain-specific capability libraries, and autonomous execution patterns without changing the canonical definition established by this specification.